# fw_env.config — libubootenv (fw_printenv / fw_setenv) for Zion Kria boards
# (KV260 / KR260, machines k26-smk-*-sdt)
#
# The Zion U-Boot for Kria (xilinx SDT machines) selects its environment
# driver at runtime from the ZynqMP boot-mode register
# (board/xilinx/zynqmp/zynqmp.c env_get_location()):
#
#   * QSPI boot (the ONLY mode Kria SOMs boot from — the boot firmware
#     lives in the QSPI "Image A"/"Image B" slots)  -> ENVL_SPI_FLASH:
#     raw binary env in the QSPI partitions
#         "U-Boot storage variables"         @ 0x2200000  (128 KiB)
#         "U-Boot storage variables backup"  @ 0x2220000  (128 KiB, redundant)
#   * SD-mode boot (not used on Kria)             -> FAT env (uboot.env)
#
# The kernel exposes the QSPI partitions as MTD devices; the redundant
# copies are required for CONFIG_SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT=y (both slots
# are written on every saveenv, so a power cut mid-write can never corrupt
# the environment).
#
# Hard-coded /dev/mtdN indices are fragile (they renumber if the device
# tree gains partitions), so 60-zion-uboot-env.rules creates stable
# symlinks from the MTD partition *names*:
#   /dev/zion/uboot-env        -> "U-Boot storage variables"
#   /dev/zion/uboot-env-redund -> "U-Boot storage variables backup"
#
# Format: <device> <offset> <env-size> <sector-size> <number-of-sectors>
# The env partition is exactly one 128 KiB QSPI erase sector.

/dev/zion/uboot-env         0x0     0x20000   0x20000   1
/dev/zion/uboot-env-redund  0x0     0x20000   0x20000   1